    },
    {
      "_id": "crGSI2ZJv6mlTGJE",
      "name": "Blind",
      "type": "specialAbility",
      "img": "systems/modern20/assets/icons/lorc/third-eye.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>A sheetlike animated object (such as a carpet or a drape) can use this ability against an opponent up to three size categories larger than itself. The animated object makes a normal grapple check. If it gets a hold, it wraps itself around the opponent\u2019s head, blinding that creature until removed. The blinded creature cannot make Search, Spot, or @Check[skill:survival]{Survival check}s to track, and it takes a \u20136 circumstance penalty on all other checks related to perception (such as Listen).</p>",
        "source": "Menace Manual",
        "srdUrl": "https://spellbooksoftware.com/d20mrsd/menacecreat1.html",
        "rulesPage": "Compendium.modern20.rules.JournalEntry.gkO7BHtoB7PZOT9Q.JournalEntryPage.QvZNL5dJUs6a3FCL",
        "abilityType": "extraordinary",
        "sense": false,
        "activities": {}
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!dMEQNiAyf7hL1aAJ.crGSI2ZJv6mlTGJE"
    },
    {
      "_id": "IAk8d3pw2jsNnxYf",
      "name": "Constrict",
      "type": "specialAbility",
      "img": "systems/modern20/assets/icons/lorc/grab.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>A flexible animated object (such as a rope or chain) deals automatic slam damage with a successful grapple check against a target up to one size category larger than itself.</p><p>A Large or larger animated object (flexible or not) can make constrict attacks against multiple creatures at once. Each of the targets of such an attack must be at least two size categories smaller than the animated object and able to fit underneath it.</p>",
        "source": "Menace Manual",
        "srdUrl": "https://spellbooksoftware.com/d20mrsd/menacecreat1.html",
        "rulesPage": "Compendium.modern20.rules.JournalEntry.gkO7BHtoB7PZOT9Q.JournalEntryPage.QvZNL5dJUs6a3FCL",
        "abilityType": "extraordinary",
        "sense": false,
        "activities": {}
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!dMEQNiAyf7hL1aAJ.IAk8d3pw2jsNnxYf"
    },
    {
      "_id": "X5sRPK0faD04kBbQ",
      "name": "Hardness",
      "type": "specialAbility",
      "img": "systems/modern20/assets/icons/lorc/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>An animated object has the same hardness it had before it was animated.</p>",
        "source": "Menace Manual",
        "srdUrl": "https://spellbooksoftware.com/d20mrsd/menacecreat1.html",
        "rulesPage": "Compendium.modern20.rules.JournalEntry.gkO7BHtoB7PZOT9Q.JournalEntryPage.QvZNL5dJUs6a3FCL",
        "abilityType": "extraordinary",
        "sense": false,
        "activities": {}
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!dMEQNiAyf7hL1aAJ.X5sRPK0faD04kBbQ"
    },
    {
      "_id": "Rc3TA2OEBkiKvfMc",
      "name": "Improved Speed",
      "type": "specialAbility",
      "img": "systems/modern20/assets/icons/lorc/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The base speeds given in the statistics blocks below assume that the animated objects lurch, rock, or slither along the ground. An object with two legs (a statue or a ladder, for example) or some other feature that allows faster movement has a bonus of +10 feet to its speed. An object with multiple legs (such as a table, chair, or statue of a quadrupedal creature) has a bonus of +20 feet, and a wheeled object has a bonus of +40 feet.</p><p>Certain objects might also have other modes of movement. A wooden object can float, so it has a swim speed equal to one-half its land speed. A rope or similar sinuous object has a climb speed equal to one-half its land speed. A sheetlike object can fly (clumsy maneuverability) at one-half its land speed.</p>",
        "source": "Menace Manual",
        "srdUrl": "https://spellbooksoftware.com/d20mrsd/menacecreat1.html",
        "rulesPage": "Compendium.modern20.rules.JournalEntry.gkO7BHtoB7PZOT9Q.JournalEntryPage.QvZNL5dJUs6a3FCL",
        "abilityType": "extraordinary",
        "sense": false,
        "activities": {}
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!dMEQNiAyf7hL1aAJ.Rc3TA2OEBkiKvfMc"
    },
    {
      "_id": "o5v3i8K0Kcj6J9w9",
      "name": "Trample",
      "type": "specialAbility",
      "img": "systems/modern20/assets/icons/delapouite/charging-bull.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>As a standard action during its turn each round, a Large or larger animated object with a hardness of at least 10 can trample opponents at least two size categories smaller than itself. This attack deals bludgeoning damage equal to the object\u2019s slam damage plus 1.5 times its Strength modifier. A trampled opponent can attempt either an attack of opportunity at a \u20134 penalty or a @Check[save:ref]{Reflex save} (DC 10 + 1/2 object\u2019s HD + object\u2019s Strength bonus) for half damage.</p>",
        "source": "Menace Manual",
        "srdUrl": "https://spellbooksoftware.com/d20mrsd/menacecreat1.html",
        "rulesPage": "Compendium.modern20.rules.JournalEntry.gkO7BHtoB7PZOT9Q.JournalEntryPage.QvZNL5dJUs6a3FCL",
        "abilityType": "extraordinary",
        "sense": false,
        "activities": {}
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!dMEQNiAyf7hL1aAJ.o5v3i8K0Kcj6J9w9"
    }
